A||||8||Brandon86SE||Alternator or Battery is shot.||||9||
Z||000000||Brandon86SE||11-30-2001||12:56 AM||||Alright, I think my alternator is gone, but looking for your guys opinion.  I was driving to the mall today to meet my mom for supper since she's in town.  Just before I got there I started having some electrical failure.  My amp/sub died, then the stereo started cutting in and out, then dash lights were getting dimmer.  But I got it parked, and had dinner and such.  Went back out to fire it up and go home (about -15 out), and it started alright, I was letting her warm up, and everything seemed alright.  Then the stereo cut out, and I got a service engine soon light.  I shut the car off, and took a look at battery connections, see if something was loose, and checked some fuses.  Well, nothing there, so I went to start it again, get it home, and figure it out tomorrow.  Well, no such luck, no start.  I got a hold of my uncle to get a boost, and that got her started, but it didn't make it 30ft before dying again.  We pushed her into a parking stall, took anything visibly valuable out, informed mall security, etc.  I just got home.  My guess is it's the alternator shot, but it might(???) just be the battery.  If someone could give me their guess that'd be great.  Also if someone could let me know how to get the alternator out of a 1986SE 2.8L 4spd if it comes to that.<P>I do plan on pulling the battery tomorrow, and getting it checked at a parts store, if it's alright, I'll be finding a new alt.  My friend tells me there's a Fiero at a junkers here, should I consider that, or go for a new one?  If new, how much would that run?  Thanks everyone, please make my day better.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>Brandon<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Field_Front_(sig)_1.jpg"> ||||reg||9
Z||000001||GT-maniac||11-30-2001||01:33 AM||||My bet would be the alternator, I had the exact same thing happen to me. The radio started cutting in and out and then the car started surging back and forth and then just suddenly died. Unfortunately I was still 50 clicks from home at the time in the middle of nowhere. Luckily I had my cell phone with me and was able to call my wife and we limped it home by boosting it every once and a while. When I took the alternator out the plastic support underneath the ring terminal was melted!. I took it back to Canadian Tire and they replaced it no problem. I then had to replace it again when it died on the way to Edmonton the night before the Red Deer run. I'm beginning to think I should just carry an extra one and tools every time I go anywhere. As for taking it out real simple if you have the 4 speed, though I've heard cars with the air conditioning compressor can be a pain. if you can find one in a wreckers that would be a lot cheaper and might be ok if it hasn't been exposed to the elements. I think I had to pay around $ 120 for my last new one at CT. They're simple to take out just disconnect the electrical, pull the two bolts and drop it out the bottom. To install just do the reverse having someone pry against the alternator to get the correct tension on the belt before tightening the bolts up.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero005a.jpg">  <P>85 WS6 GT partly modified<BR>87 GT Loaded resto project<p>[This message has been edited by GT-maniac (edited 11-30-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||fierospeeder||11-30-2001||01:37 AM||||im positive all fieros had the volt gauge.<P><BR>tomorrow, turn your key and see what your volt gauge says.  should be 11/12 volts.<BR>because your battery is a bit drained it might be 10/11 volts.<P>Get your uncle to jump you.  While your car is running.  Look at what your volt is reading.  It should be 14/15 volts if its charging and you got a good clue that your alternator is okay.   If its saying 12volts that means your alt is bad.  <P>Also, another test is.  Turn off your car and see what the volt is when you turn the key on.  Has there been an increase of voltage.  Did the battery held a charge?<P>goodluck <P>i went through alternators on my tbird and its not fun having a car die out miles from home.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Master_Sushi||11-30-2001||01:52 AM||||Wow, I just got to walk 3 miles in cold rain last night after my alternator died on me! Alternator and battery both new will be like 150$. If I were you I'd just get both(unless battory is somewhat new and tests fine). Last thing you want is a break down somewhere because you used old crap parts. I had the alternator and battery both die in my last fiero also  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif">. They seem to go around the same time. Never installed a alternator in a V6, but the 4 cyl are easy. Maybe a few hours of work.||||reg||14
Z||000004||Master_Sushi||11-30-2001||01:56 AM||||My 88 coupe didn't have a volt meter. Most fieros do though. I like to have one myself. idiot light dosen't tell me enough.<P>My 84 coupe has one and the car was runing all the way down to 7 volts! It was really chuging and bucking at that point, but I wasn't stoping for anything.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Pyric||11-30-2001||06:28 AM||||Yeah, I had a similar problem.  Every time I would stomp on the brakes, the car would stall.  Turned out the alternator had been slowly dying. Eventually it died and 3 days later my battery ran out of power.  <P>I saw it coming when the dash lights started dimming and the stereo cut out.   It was like a race with the devil to get as close to home as I could.||||reg||1
Z||000006||rogergarrison||11-30-2001||06:43 AM||||you can just hook a voltmeter to the alt and see if its charging. should be between 13.5 and 14.5 volts with everything on and at a fast idle. Autozone has a lifetime alt for $69 (thats as long as you own it, they give you new one) And I never pay more than $50 for a battery. They give up usually at 4 or 5 years no matter how much they cost.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Brandon86SE||11-30-2001||06:48 PM||||Just to let everyone know, I pulled the battery today and got it tested, hooped.  So I got a new one, and just drove the car home!  Everything seems good now!  Bastards at Canadian Tire knew my battery was only like 2 years old, but wouldn't do a DAMN thing for me even after putting up quite an argument.  It had a 6 year warranty.  Oh well, she's running again.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Brandon||||reg||1
Z||000008||rogergarrison||11-30-2001||08:34 PM||||see, told ya to buy just a cheap one. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> $39 one lasted 2 years more than $165 one did in my mercedes.||||reg||1
